   and the Actions board, the task panel, the Job File and the TV all ask for it. The last result lives in data table cbs_cache (key 'jobreqs'),
   which every run sees immediately (workflow static data only saves when a run ends, so concurrent runs could not see each other).
   - result younger than 10 minutes: returned at once (JR Warm recalculates every 2 minutes in working hours, Mon-Sat 6am-8pm,
     so callers never wait for the slow recalculation; outside those hours a result older than 10 minutes is recalculated here)
   - a recalculation already running (busy_at younger than 4 minutes): the last result is returned at once, however old, instead of starting another
   - otherwise this run marks busy (JR Mark Busy), recalculates, and JR Store saves the result and clears busy
   body {fresh:1} skips the 3-minute copy, but never starts a second recalculation while one is running. */
